  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Demolition of the existing side extension and excavation of basement, erection of a double storey side extension with front and rear lightwells alongside alterations to the existing rear extension&nbsp;",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed rear ground floor extension, by reason of its excessive height and scale, would fail to appear subordinate to the host building. The extension would result in an overly dominant and bulky addition that harms the architectural character of the property.&amp;nbsp; The proposal therefore fails to respect the character and appearance of the area, contrary to policies D1 (&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;London’s form, character and capacity for growth),&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;D3&amp;nbsp; (&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach) &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;and D4 (Delivering good design) of the London Plan (2021), policies LP1 (&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Design Quality and Local Character&lt;/span&gt;) and LP17 (Housing Design) of the Hackney Local Plan (2020), and the Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2025).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development would result in substandard and poor-quality accommodation for future occupiers, particularly within Flat 2. By virtue of its excessive size and subterranean location, the proposed basement kitchen would fail to provide adequate natural daylight, sunlight, or a meaningful external outlook, resulting in an oppressive living environment. Furthermore, the introduction of a lightwell to serve this kitchen significantly reduces the usability and quality of the private rear garden. The proposal, therefore, represents an over-development of the site that would be detrimental to the long-term health and well-being of occupants, contrary to policy D6 (Housing standards) of the London Plan (2021) and policies LP1 (&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Design Quality and Local Character) &lt;/span&gt;and LP17 (Housing Design) of the Hackney Local Plan (2020) and Hackney&#x27;s Residential Alterations and Extensions SPD (2025).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
